ARCHITECTURE NOTE (honesty): the web source is an UNROUTED card grid the Automations builder embeds; its one data
hook is useAutomationPresets(category) -> GET /automations/presets[?category=]. The presentational + projection
surface was already implemented at full parity by the predecessor prompt p3-android/feature-views A-0085-PresetGallery
(log p3-android-feature-views-0085-PresetGallery.log; com/teslasync/feature-views/PresetGallery, committed + green;
fv unit test PresetGalleryProjectionTest + UI test PresetGalleryUiTest already in the suite). This page prompt targets
the separate allowed-files path kotlin/com/teslasync/automations/** with a `@Composable screen + ViewModel` contract,
so — following the sanctioned ConditionBuilder / AutomationCard precedent — this layer is a THIN page wrapper that
EMBEDS that one shared surface (every panel/string/data state is the parity-covered feature view's PresetGalleryContent)
and adds only the page state holder + the stateless screen. Predecessor NOT bypassed.

DATA-SOURCE NOTE (honesty): the surface declares one data source — useAutomationPresets (GET /automations/presets
[?category=]). It is bound through the shared S8 AutomationsStore.automationPresets(category) via the page-layer
PresetGallerySource seam (presetGallerySource(store, category)); the page ViewModel only re-shares that
cache-then-network feed onto UiState through the shared BaseFeedViewModel.asUiState helper (the standard A7 page-VM
job). The shared-core AutomationPreset rows are projected to the feature view's vendor-neutral AutomationPresetData at
that boundary (PresetGalleryPageModel.toPresetData/wireKind) because the page module cannot widen the feature-view
directory (outside this prompt's allowed files); this is exactly the host-side adaptation the fv model documents. No
HTTP, no business logic, no re-implementation of the preset fetch is added by this layer.

NAV NOTE (honesty): web route is "(unrouted)". Destinations.kt is the canonical registry — "every web route recorded
as metadata … never any fabricated stand-in", and DestinationsTest.registryCoversTheWholeWebTaxonomy() locks
Destinations.all to the web taxonomy while RouteTableTest round-trips every Destinations.all entry. An unrouted card
grid has no web route, so NO synthetic nav destination is fabricated (doing so would break the locked tests and the
registry's anti-fabrication contract). The page-layer is embedded by the Automations builder exactly as the feature
view is — the prompt's "(if routed)" clause does not apply, identical to the sibling AutomationCard / ConditionBuilder
pages.

GATE PATH NOTE: the project Gradle path is ':android' (settings.gradle.kts maps ':android' -> app/); the prompt
snippet's ':app:' is the same module (documented alias, as in every sibling P3/A* gate log).

